This confocal microscopy image (Fig. 4) illustrates the enhanced uptake of antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs) when formulated with Nano-11 nanoparticles. BMDCs incubated with soluble ovalbumin (OVA) show minimal uptake, while those incubated with AF647-labeled Nano-11 (red) demonstrate efficient internalization. Crucially, when OVA (green) is adsorbed to Nano-11, its uptake by BMDCs is significantly increased, with both components colocalizing within the cells, highlighting Nano-11's role in effective antigen delivery.